digraph guide { graph [pad=0.5]; node [shape=plain, fontname="Liberation Sans", fontsize=16]; guide [label="PostgreSQL database diagrams\n\n105 tables, 610 columns (including inherited columns), 110 foreign-key constraints, 2 inheritance relationships.\n\nSource: Eddict/tmp / pgsql_db.sql\n\nPK: primary key    FK: foreign key    ?: nullable    *: inherited column\nU1, U2, ...: unique key/index groups local to each table.\nColumns with the same U number form one composite key.\n\nArrows: foreign-key columns -> referenced columns (not crow's-foot notation).\nDashed arrows: PostgreSQL INHERITS, not a foreign key.\nGray tables: cross-group references, showing primary and referenced columns only.\nAll other tables show all columns, including inherited columns.\n\nOnly declared foreign keys are drawn. Similar column names do not imply a link.\nDefaults, checks, triggers, functions, non-unique indexes and runtime tables are omitted.\n\nMedia and files\nMetadata and geography\nAlbums, sharing and favorites\nPeople and face recognition\nTags, concepts and search\nSimilar media\nUsers and permissions\nProcessing and background tasks\nEvents and version tracking\nConfiguration, temporary and test tables"]; }